# Immigrant Application System (Enterprise Architecture Upgrade)

## Project Origin & Attribution
This application originally started as a collaborative academic project for CS321 at George Mason University.
* **Original Application Scope:** Initial Java backend services, database mappings, and core logic queues.
* **Original Contributors:** Mostafa Mahtab, Shane Brickhead, Kavon Barr.

## Individual Enterprise Upgrades (By Mostafa Mahtab)
This repository represents an independent, production-grade re-architecture of the original system to bridge the gap between academic code and cloud-portable DevOps standards:
* **Multi-Container Micro-Services:** Containerized the app using Docker and Docker Compose stacks.
* **Database Volume Persistence:** Configured named Docker volumes to permanently anchor MySQL data on host disk tracks.
* **Nginx Reverse Proxy Gateway:** Integrated an Nginx proxy layer to process secure connection routing over web port 80.
* **Automated CI/CD Pipeline:** Built a GitHub Actions workflow that executes checkstyle quality gates and runs the 11 unit tests automatically on push.





