Under model sub package -

AlienRelative.java - define all the private fields and the getter and setter methods for alien relatives, helps map their information in the database columns. The primary key is the id which is reflected in the database.

ImmigrantEntity.java - Defines the private fields and getter and setters for the primary immigrant applicant. The primary key is the applicantId or the 9 digits unique A- number (system generated). This file also maps the client relatives with their associated primary applicant using list data structure.


Under repository sub-package -

AlienRelativeRepository.java - it defines the AlienRelativeRepository interface force implementing List data structure where we find alien relative by their ID (shows up in the database)

ImmigrantRepository.java - it defines interface ImmigrantRepository and force implementation of List data structure where we can identify the primary immigrant by their form status in the workflow and their full name.


Under service sub-package -

ImmigrantService.java - helps with all the status update services throughout the workflow once the UI users (data entry, reviewer, approver) submits their form. The status update occurs in real time in the database once the correct commands are run.

This file has been removed for the iteration 6 final submission as we do not need to actually send email -
NotificationService.java - this form should help with  the notifications sending modules to reviewer or applicant depending on  disapproval or approval.

ErrorCode.java - this file defines all the error codes.

Immigrant.java - this is the Immigrant class. It implements Hash Map data structure, defines private fields, define constructor, create Immigrant object, help update immigrant entry field information, defines getters methods, and returns the unique A- number.


ImmigrantApplication.java - this has the main method in it. It helps run the whole system.

ImmigrantException.java - this file helps throw error code if any problem occurs in the workflow.


Under resources/static sub-packages -

approver-queue.html - define the skeleton of the approver facing queue UI the asynchronous function fetch the form submitted by the reviewer and load the queue for the approver.

dataEntry-review_queue.html - define the skeleton of the dataEntry to reviewer queue which is reviewer facing UI, the asynchronous function help load and fetch the form submitted by the data-entry clerk.

immigrant-approver.html -  this defines the main UI for the approver where the approver can approver or disapprover of the forms submitted by the reviewer. This UI fetches all the submitted forms and show them one by one, make the buttons logic work for approval or disapproval (force to leave a reason for disapproval).


immigrant-data_entry.html - define the skeletons - buttons and data fields for the data-entry clerk UI. The save asynchronous function help with saving the data in the database, updates the status in the database, and show alert that it was submitted to data- entry to reviewer queue.

reviewer.html - help define the skeleton - buttons and data-fields for the reviewer facing main UI page. The asynchronous function loadForm loads the form for the reviewer same as submitted by the data-entry clerk, save asynchronous function help with saving the data in the database, updates the status in the database, and show alert that it was submitted to approver queue.


